        {"name": "micron::math::cr::ziv_result", "header": "math/cr.hpp", "summary": "Double-double approximation y and asserted absolute-error bound abs_err for a rounding-test stage.", "sections": [s("Driver behavior", "drive_f64/drive_f64_2arg run a first stage, test, then a second stage if needed and return that stage even if its test remains inconclusive. Binary32 drivers round the supplied double-double stage through a round-to-odd helper. Specific sin/cos/log/exp CR routines use bounded double-double kernels rather than an extensible precision ladder. This record is useful for the stage protocol, not an independent proof that an arbitrary supplied error bound is valid.")]},
